(452, 1, '2023-05-13 07:54:56', '2023-05-13 07:54:56', '<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Bringing Joy and Education to Underprivileged Children</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"textColor\":\"luminous-vivid-orange\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-luminous-vivid-orange-color has-text-color\">Ramdhanu - The Colour of Hope is a project that aims to bring hope and joy to underprivileged children living on the streets. </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The project was founded during the pandemic when many of these children lost all hope and were struggling to even arrange two square meals a day. Mitrobinda Ghosh, the founder, started by giving them colors and papers to create rainbows out of the darkness and pain, and thus Ramdhanu - The Colour of Hope was born.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The project began with just four children, but soon grew to include 24 street children and three volunteers who are still an important part of the organization. The project provides access to education, healthcare, nutrition, and basic hygiene for these children, and aims to break the cycle of poverty by empowering the community through sustainable programs. The project also works to raise awareness about the needs of underprivileged children and advocate for their rights. Ramdhanu - The Colour of Hope is more than just a project, it\'s a beacon of hope for those who have been left behind by society.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->', 'Color Of Hope', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '50-revision-v1', '', '', '2023-05-13 07:54:56', '2023-05-13 07:54:56', '', 50, 'http://localhost/ramdhanu-website/?p=452', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(453, 1, '2023-05-13 07:57:47', '2023-05-13 07:57:47', '<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Our cultural program events are a celebration of various festivals throughout the year. We bring smiles to as many children as we can by organizing various activities during festivals such as Durga Pujo, Christmas, Holi, and Poila Boishakh. We gift them new clothes, bags, and stationery, take them to restaurants, organize sit and draw competitions, and offer food. For Holi, we hosted a storytelling event and concluded with playing Holi. For Poila Boishakh, we gift them traditional clothes and organize cultural activities such as dancing, singing, and poetry recitation. Our cultural events aim to nurture tradition and culture while bringing joy and happiness to the children.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->', 'Culture Programs', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '315-revision-v1', '', '', '2023-05-13 07:57:47', '2023-05-13 07:57:47', '', 315, 'http://localhost/ramdhanu-website/?p=453', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(454, 1, '2023-05-13 07:59:10', '2023-05-13 07:59:10', '<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Ramdhanu organizes quarterly health checkups for street children, with the assistance of renowned practicing doctors. Our medical team comprises Doyel Dey, a qualified nurse working in a government hospital, and Dr. Nibedita Manna, an MD in Pediatrics. During the checkups, we primarily evaluate the kids\' nutrition levels, report any minor health concerns to the doctors, and take necessary actions such as buying them required medications, conducting further checkups, or admitting them to hospitals. Additionally, we provide the children with prescribed nutritional supplements like vitamin gummies and calcium tablets. Join us in ensuring the well-being of these precious children.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->', 'Medical Camp', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '343-revision-v1', '', '', '2023-05-13 07:59:10', '2023-05-13 07:59:10', '', 343, 'http://localhost/ramdhanu-website/?p=454', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(455, 1, '2023-05-13 08:00:24', '2023-05-13 08:00:24', '<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Ramdhanu annually celebrates Children\'s Day by organizing a sports event for the street children. The event includes various fun competitions and games such as running, frog jumping, marble and spoon race, as well as intellectual challenges like memory games. Winners are awarded medals and prizes, and the day concludes with food and juices. Additionally, Ramdhanu conducts Yoga workshops on International Yoga Day to spread awareness of the benefits of yoga among underprivileged children and includes yoga as part of their education plan. Ramdhanu also regularly organizes self-defense classes, especially for girls, to teach children how to defend themselves and fight off intruders with the help of Sreejata Dutta, a 1st dan black belt Taekwondo artist.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->', 'Sports Events', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '356-revision-v1', '', '', '2023-05-13 08:00:24', '2023-05-13 08:00:24', '', 356, 'http://localhost/ramdhanu-website/?p=455', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(456, 1, '2023-05-13 08:01:46', '2023-05-13 08:01:46', '<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Ramdhanu strongly believes in collaborations and hence collaborates with various organizations to reach out to more underprivileged children. The Rotaract Club is one such organization with which Ramdhanu frequently collaborates to organize events for children living on the streets, providing them with clothes, food, and educational stationery. Additionally, Ramdhanu also collaborated with Akshar School for their \"Each One Teach One\" project, where students of Akshar School came to teach and participate in various events for Ramdhanu\'s children. Akshar School teachers also regularly joined in to teach, take workshops, and distribute school stationary and food. Ramdhanu\'s children were even given the opportunity to showcase their talent in Heritage School\'s prestigious event, \"Youthopia by Heritage School\", where three of Ramdhanu\'s children performed in front of a thousand audiences for the first time.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->', 'Collaborations', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '302-revision-v1', '', '', '2023-05-13 08:01:46', '2023-05-13 08:01:46', '', 302, 'http://localhost/ramdhanu-website/?p=456', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
