(972, 1, '2025-08-11 08:26:12', '2025-08-11 08:26:12', '<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Pavement to Possibilities: A Pathway to a Brighter Future</h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Pavement to Possibilities—where hope finds its footing on the streets. Born from lived experience and compassion, it’s a vital initiative of Ramdhanu, addressing the silent suffering of street children, elderly homeless individuals, and disabled people who survive under harsh conditions. Recognizing the forgotten lives on the pavements, we began with a single, crucial step – to offer support and ignite a spark of opportunity.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Our initiative transforms pavements into classrooms, with dedicated interns and experienced educators providing education and essential resources. Alongside lessons and warm, nutritious meals, we offer emotional support – planting seeds of hope in places often left forgotten. Every week, we distribute food packets and provide critical supplies like blankets, umbrellas, and raincoats, offering a lifeline against the elements.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Ultimately, Pavement to Possibilities is about recognizing that every individual deserves dignity and opportunity. We strive to tell each person: \'You are not invisible. You are not forgotten.’ With the enrollment of many children in mainstream schools and the continued weekly support, we’re confident in our mission to leave no one behind on the pavement—where possibility still resides. </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->', 'Pavement to Possibilities', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '937-revision-v1', '', '', '2025-08-11 08:26:12', '2025-08-11 08:26:12', '', 937, 'http://localhost/ramdhanu-website/?p=972', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(973, 1, '2025-08-11 10:56:55', '2025-08-11 10:56:55', '<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Restoring Dignity: Ramdhanu’s Fight Against Period Poverty</h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Period poverty – the absence of access to sanitary products – isn’t just a lack of supplies; it’s a barrier to education, health, and dignity for countless girls and women. In many parts of India, menstruation is shrouded in silence and shame, leading to harmful practices and significant health risks, particularly for marginalized communities.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Ramdhanu’s ‘Period Poverty Movement’ directly addresses this injustice. We regularly distribute sanitary napkins to girls in schools across Kolkata and empower young women living on the streets. Our dedicated team organizes awareness sessions, bringing in medical experts to educate on menstrual health and break harmful stigmas.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>But our commitment extends beyond the city. In tribal villages, we replicate this approach – distributing products, facilitating open conversations, and fostering a culture of pride and self-care. Through every pad provided, every conversation sparked, and every stigma challenged, we’re restoring dignity and building a future where periods are no longer a barrier to opportunity and well-being.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->', 'Period Poverty', '', 'publish', 'closed', 'closed', '', 'period-poverty', '', '', '2025-08-11 13:37:54', '2025-08-11 13:37:54', '', 0, 'http://localhost/ramdhanu-website/?page_id=973', 0, 'page', '', 0),
